ludeTo":true,"label":"At or above the screening threshold","source":"https://license.tov.med.nyu.edu/product/asrs6Qscreener","to":6}],"basis":"screening","code":"below_screen","construct":"Qualifying shaded responses","continuous":false,"currentBand":{"code":"below_screen","from":0,"includeFrom":true,"includeTo":true,"label":"Below the screening threshold","source":"https://license.tov.med.nyu.edu/product/asrs6Qscreener","to":3},"displayKind":"screening-count","label":"Below the screening threshold","limitations":["The published range belongs to this instrument; it does not establish a diagnosis, cause or probability of a condition."],"meaning":"Qualifying shaded responses: {{value}} (0–6). Holistic House explanation: {{value}} of 6 answers fall in the shaded cells under the classic ASRS-v1.1 rule for the past 6 months. A result of 0–3 is below the screening threshold but does not rule out ADHD. This is not a diagnosis, severity rating or probability of a condition. Discuss any concerns with a qualified healthcare professional regardless of the result. The questionnaire uses the original English form.","presentationDirection":"difficulty","recommendedReview":false,"reliableDirection":true,"source":"https://license.tov.med.nyu.edu/product/asrs6Qscreener","summary":"The result is below the screening threshold but does not rule out ADHD. This is not a diagnosis or severity rating. Discuss concerning symptoms with a qualified professional regardless of the score.","verified":true},"values":[0,1,2,3]},{"template":{"actions":["At {{value}} (0–6), the category is At or above the screening threshold. Discuss symptoms and their effect on daily life with a qualified professional; the questionnaire does not determine a diagnosis or treatment.","Consider noting concrete examples of attention or activity difficulties and their effect on daily life to discuss with a qualified healthcare professional."],"bands":[{"code":"below_screen","from":0,"includeFrom":true,"includeTo":true,"label":"Below the screening threshold","source":"https://license.tov.med.nyu.edu/product/asrs6Qscreener","to":3},{"code":"screen_signal","from":4,"includeFrom":true,"includeTo":true,"label":"At or above the screening threshold","source":"https://license.tov.med.nyu.edu/product/asrs6Qscreener","to":6}],"basis":"screening","code":"screen_signal","construct":"Qualifying shaded responses","continuous":false,"currentBand":{"code":"screen_signal","from":4,"includeFrom":true,"includeTo":true,"label":"At or above the screening threshold","source":"https://license.tov.med.nyu.edu/product/asrs6Qscreener","to":6},"displayKind":"screening-count","label":"At or above the screening threshold","limitations":["The published range belongs to this instrument; it does not establish a diagnosis, cause or probability of a condition."],"meaning":"Qualifying shaded responses: {{value}} (0–6). Holistic House explanation: {{value}} of 6 answers fall in the shaded cells under the classic ASRS-v1.1 rule for the past 6 months. A result of 4–6 indicates symptoms that may be consistent with adult ADHD. It may be helpful to discuss an evaluation with a qualified healthcare professional. This is not a diagnosis, severity rating or probability of a condition. Discuss any concerns with a qualified healthcare professional regardless of the result. The questionnaire uses the original English form.","presentationDirection":"difficulty","recommendedReview":true,"reliableDirection":true,"source":"https://license.tov.med.nyu.edu/product/asrs6Qscreener","summary":"The result is at or above the screening threshold: symptoms may be consistent with adult ADHD. This is not a diagnosis or severity rating. Discuss concerning symptoms with a qualified professional regardless of the score.","verified":true},"values":[4,5,6]}]}],"discoveryClassification":{"basis":"discovery-only-not-clinical-validation","kind":"professional","policySource":"lib/assessments/test-kinds.js","policySourceCommit":"d9ba8b92eb7bff99864d54