nosis, norm or percentile."],"meaning":"Emotional volatility: {{value}} (1–5). Higher scores describe becoming irritated, upset or emotionally stirred up more readily; lower scores describe steadier composure. This aspect concerns emotional reactivity, not whether feelings are justified or whether someone is dangerous. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles. Mean of 10 responses, after reversing the items specified by the key. No verified clinical categories are assigned to this result here.","presentationDirection":"neutral","recommendedReview":false,"reliableDirection":true,"source":"https://ipip.ori.org/BFASKeys.htm","summary":"Higher scores describe becoming irritated, upset or emotionally stirred up more readily; lower scores describe steadier composure. This aspect concerns emotional reactivity, not whether feelings are justified or whether someone is dangerous. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles.","verified":true},"values":[1,1.1,1.2,1.3,1.4,1.5,1.6,1.7,1.8,1.9,2,2.1,2.2,2.3,2.4,2.5,2.6,2.7,2.8,2.9,3,3.1,3.2,3.3,3.4,3.5,3.6,3.7,3.8,3.9,4,4.1,4.2,4.3,4.4,4.5,4.6,4.7,4.8,4.9,5]}]}],"discoveryClassification":{"basis":"discovery-only-not-clinical-validation","kind":"professional","policySource":"lib/assessments/test-kinds.js","policySourceCommit":"d9ba8b92eb7bff99864d5403d9a78a199b727892","policySourceSha256":"sha256:77c573884f78cdc8c4fb58b15990dcce50218c4b6666a89c1ffe2fe8a4142167"},"interpretationVersion":"2026-10-17.v1","provenance":{"assessmentVersionId":"d6277cc3-f343-5576-afc4-2a4717387448","contentHash":"sha256:ae14c686ba6291bbe82550dfc4d2936ac7897d389439b9a5c654bb7f9d097154","definitionKey":"ipip-aspect-volatility-10","definitionVersion":"v1","instrumentLocale":"en","resultVe