iation of beauty: {{value}} (1–5). Higher scores describe more noticing and emotional response to beauty, including in nature; lower scores describe less of that reported attention. This does not test artistic taste or imply an obligation to enjoy art. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles. Mean of 4 responses, after reversing the items specified by the key. No verified clinical categories are assigned to this result here.","presentationDirection":"neutral","recommendedReview":false,"reliableDirection":true,"source":"https://ipip.ori.org/IPIP-VIA-R_Key.html","summary":"Higher scores describe more noticing and emotional response to beauty, including in nature; lower scores describe less of that reported attention. This does not test artistic taste or imply an obligation to enjoy art. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles.","verified":true},"values":[1,1.25,1.5,1.75,2,2.25,2.5,2.75,3,3.25,3.5,3.75,4,4.25,4.5,4.75,5]}]}],"discoveryClassification":{"basis":"discovery-only-not-clinical-validation","kind":"professional","policySource":"lib/assessments/test-kinds.js","policySourceCommit":"d9ba8b92eb7bff99864d5403d9a78a199b727892","policySourceSha256":"sha256:77c573884f78cdc8c4fb58b15990dcce50218c4b6666a89c1ffe2fe8a4142167"},"interpretationVersion":"2026-10-17.v1","provenance":{"assessmentVersionId":"4282c169-808a-5a23-9c3e-bac9d2696a8d","contentHash":"sha256:803f2b30412509f8a40861ce8cb34adb04285a78c17668f1438902e84cd4bb31","definitionKey":"ipip-via-r-appreciation-beauty-4","definitionVersion":"v1","instrumentLocale":"en","resultVersion":"v1","scoringKey":"configured","scoringVersion":"v1","translationVersion":"original-en-v1"},"rendererStrategy":"finite-domain-template.v1","reportLocale":"en","