 scores describe more willingness to state beliefs and unpopular opinions despite opposition; lower scores describe more reluctance when consequences are possible. These items concern speaking up, not all forms of courage or willingness to face physical danger. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles. Mean of 4 responses, after reversing the items specified by the key. No verified clinical categories are assigned to this result here.","presentationDirection":"neutral","recommendedReview":false,"reliableDirection":true,"source":"https://ipip.ori.org/IPIP-VIA-R_Key.html","summary":"Higher scores describe more willingness to state beliefs and unpopular opinions despite opposition; lower scores describe more reluctance when consequences are possible. These items concern speaking up, not all forms of courage or willingness to face physical danger. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles.","verified":true},"values":[1,1.25,1.5,1.75,2,2.25,2.5,2.75,3,3.25,3.5,3.75,4,4.25,4.5,4.75,5]}]}],"discoveryClassification":{"basis":"discovery-only-not-clinical-validation","kind":"professional","policySource":"lib/assessments/test-kinds.js","policySourceCommit":"d9ba8b92eb7bff99864d5403d9a78a199b727892","policySourceSha256":"sha256:77c573884f78cdc8c4fb58b15990dcce50218c4b6666a89c1ffe2fe8a4142167"},"interpretationVersion":"2026-10-17.v1","provenance":{"assessmentVersionId":"c239828d-da4c-5de2-9e50-aa38fad4ad32","contentHash":"sha256:bc7261e9a3b92dcb97e1d89384f5246f1b692cf426dacaf6250bee772da4620b","definitionKey":"ipip-via-r-bravery-4","definitionVersion":"v1","instrumentLocale":"en","resultVersion":"v1","scoringKey":"configured","scoringVersion":"v1","translationVersion":"original-en-v1"},"rendererStrategy":"f