ems specified by the key. No verified clinical categories are assigned to this result here.","presentationDirection":"neutral","recommendedReview":false,"reliableDirection":true,"source":"https://ipip.ori.org/IPIP-VIA-R_Key.html","summary":"Higher scores describe more identification with spirituality, purpose and belief in a universal power or God; lower scores describe less agreement with this combination. The scale combines distinct beliefs and is not a measure of morality, mental health or meaning available to a secular person. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles.","verified":true},"values":[1,1.25,1.5,1.75,2,2.25,2.5,2.75,3,3.25,3.5,3.75,4,4.25,4.5,4.75,5]}]},{"allowedValues":[1,1.25,1.5,1.75,2,2.25,2.5,2.75,3,3.25,3.5,3.75,4,4.25,4.5,4.75,5],"mode":"descriptive","signature":{"dimensionClass":"trait","direction":"non-normative","key":"trait.via.teamwork","max":5,"min":1,"sourceConstruct":"Teamwork and loyalty","timeframe":"general-self-description","unit":"points"},"source":"https://ipip.ori.org/IPIP-VIA-R_Key.html","variants":[{"template":{"actions":["For {{value}} (1–5) on teamwork and loyalty, record a situation that fits this description and an exception. Explore flexibility rather than aiming for a “correct” score.","If useful: In a group task, clarify roles and how to ask for help while preserving the option to disagree."],"bands":[],"basis":"descriptive","code":"continuous","construct":"Teamwork and loyalty","continuous":true,"currentBand":null,"label":"Descriptive score (1–5)","limitations":["No verified categorical cutoffs are applied to this version here. The score is not a diagnosis, norm or percentile."],"meaning":"Teamwork and loyalty: {{value}} (1–5). Higher scores describe more loyalty, support for group members and comfort working together; lower scores describe more preference for working alone or difficulty in groups. The score does not require loyalty to an unsafe or unfair group. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles. Mean of 4 responses, after reversing the items specified by the key. No verified clinical categories are assigned to this result here.","presentationDirection":"neutral","recommendedReview":false,"reliableDirection":true,"source":"https://ipip.ori.org/IPIP-VIA-R_Key.html","summary":"Higher scores describe more loyalty, support for group members and comfort working together; lower scores describe more preference for working alone or difficulty in groups. The score does not require loyalty to an unsafe or unfair group. This continuous self-description uses Holistic House explanatory prose, not a validated interpretation category; scale endpoints describe possible scores, not norms or percentiles.","verified":true},"values":[1,1.25,1.5,1.75,2,2.25,2.5,2.75,3,3.25,3.5,3.75,4,4.25,4.5,4.75,5]}]},{"allowedValues":[1,1.25,1.5,1.75,2,2.25,2.5,2.75,3,3.25,3.5,3.75,4,4.25,4.5,4.75,5],"mode":"descriptive","signature":{"dimensionClass":"trait","direction":"non-normative","key":"trait.via.zest","max":5,"min":1,"sourceConstruct":"Vitality / zest","timeframe":"general-self-description","unit":"points"},"source":"https://ipip.ori.org/IPIP-VIA-R_Key.html","variants":[{"template":{"actions":["For {{value}} (1–5) on vitality / zest, record a situation that fits this description and an exception. Explore flexibility rather than aiming for a “correct” score.","If useful: Notice which activities restore or drain energy and allow recovery; persistent unexplained exhaustion is worth discussing with a qualified clinician."],"bands":[],"basis":"descriptive","code":"continuous","construct":"Vitality / zest","continuous":true,"currentBand":null,"label":"Descriptive score (1–5)","limitations":["No verified categorical cutoffs are applied